<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jalal al-Mulk Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1099">1099</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Jalal al-Mulk Ali ibn Ammar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jalal al-Mulk Ali was the emir of Tripoli in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> from 1072 to 1099, of the Shia Banu Ammar family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qadi">qadis</a>. He extended the family's rule along the Levantine coast and kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a> independent by balancing between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>. Under the Banu Ammar Tripoli was a centre of learning, with a famous library in its Dar al-Ilm.</p></div>
